SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] Preventing & Choking in Older Adults
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nMichelle Kanevsky\, a licensed\, 
 ASHA-certified Speech-Language Pathologist who specializes in adult medical 
 speech therapy\, will explain how our throat muscles work and provide us 
 with the tools to enjoy our meals safely\, confidently\, and 
 independently.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by the MILL. Please 
 register for classes directly through their website here.\n\nFor questions 
 about MILL classes please call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is made possible 
 through a partnership between the MILL\, Montclair Public Library and 
 Partners for Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Health & Wellness
UID:LibCal-10306-16678832
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16678832
END:VEVENT
