SUMMARY:Art Talk: Deborah Ugoretz
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T140000
DTSTAMP:20261111T180315Z
UID:TU2178208084
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T123000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260929T221207Z
DESCRIPTION:https://deborahugoretz.com  \nIG:@debugoretz  \n@ketubah\\_for
 \\_life\n\nDeborah Ugoretz is a master paper-cutter with 40 years of exper
 ience facilitating workshops and classes on Jewish paåpercutting and Hebr
 ew illuminated manuscripts. Deborah has shown her work in galleries and mu
 seums across New York City and the US\, and has served as a leader in arti
 st communities as a curator for Yiddish New York and organizer of Red Hook
  Open Studios. In 2024\, she was awarded a Folk Arts Fellowship by NY Coun
 cil on the Arts and the New York Foundation for the Arts.  \n  \nDeborah s
 hares her skill as an educator\, most recently at the New School\, Nationa
 l Yiddish Book Center\, Yeshiva University Museum\, the Museum at Eldridge
  Street\, New York and at Fordham University where a retrospective of her 
 cut paper work was exhibited. For eight years\, Deborah produced an Artis
 t *Beit Midrash*\, a workshop where artists generate new work in dialogue 
 with Jewish texts and scholarship. Deborah was also a mentor in the art of
  Jewish papercutting through a grant from the New Jersey State Council for
  the Arts.  \n  \nIn papercutting\, Deborah found a way to merge her work 
 as an artist and her Jewish heritage. “I began to search through texts\,
  through the Bible and prayer for visual imagery\,” she said. “Through
  that search\, I began to discover how rich and full these writings were.
   I wanted to communicate that wealth by releasing the words\, through my
  art\, into pictorial space". Her interest in Jewish marriage contracts (*
 ketubot*) led her to study Hebrew and English calligraphy and the art of i
 lluminated manuscripts.  \n  \nUgoretz creates work in cut paper for organ
 izations and book covers\, Jewish marriage contracts. She also paints with
  acrylics and builds mobiles\, small scale boxes and screens in her studio
  in Red Hook\, Brooklyn.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261022T161219Z
LOCATION:Gallery
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL;VALUE=URI:https://teamup.com/kstx8swyw669kakgqa/events/2178208084
X-SOURCE:Congregation Shomrei Emunah
X-TEAMUP-ROOM:Gallery
END:VEVENT
