SUMMARY:Open Book\, Open Mind\; Patrick Radden Keefe\, "London Falling: A Mysterious Death in a Gilded City and a Family's Search for Truth"
DESCRIPTION:NEW VENUE! Two New Yorker staff writers in conversation! The 
 bestselling\, prize-winning author of "Say Nothing" and "Empire of Pain\," 
 Patrick Radden Keefe will talk about his new true crime account\, "London 
 Falling\," with D.T. Max ("Finale"). When a 19-year-old boy fell to his 
 death in the Thames early one morning\, his grieving family discovered the 
 secret life which had drawn him into the criminal underworld that lies 
 beneath London’s surface. \n\nThis is a ticketed event at the Unitarian 
 Universalist Congregation at Montclair. Tickets cost $40 and include a 
 pre-signed copy of the book. Register at tinyurl.com/OBOMKeefe26  Books 
 will be available for pickup at Watchung Booksellers from or you can pick 
 up your copy of the book on November 17.  Doors open at 6:30 p.m.\n\n“A 
 19-year-old man posing as the son of a Russian oligarch leaps to his death 
 from a luxury apartment on the River Thames. That's the heart-stopping 
 opening of Patrick Radden Keefe's 'London Falling.' Keefe investigates the 
 death of the young imposter\, as well as the role modern London played in 
 his demise...Keefe is an exhaustive investigative reporter who spins 
 seamless tales. He also uses the man's mysterious death to explore the 
 criminal culture that lies just beneath the glittering surface of Britain's 
 capital...London Falling rings true.--NPR\n\nOpen Book / Open Mind is 
 sponsored by Montclair Public Library Foundation\, Watchung Booksellers\, 
 Anonymous\, David and Mary Lee Jones\, and our individual Underwriters. We 
 are also grateful for the generous support of our in-kind sponsors\, First 
 Congregational Church of Montclair\, The George\, and Amanti Vino. To 
 support Open Book / Open Mind and other library programs\, click here to 
 donate.
LOCATION:Montclair - Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Montclair\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Open Book / Open Mind
UID:LibCal-10306-16474931
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16474931
END:VEVENT
