DTEND:20261119T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20261118T000000Z
SUMMARY:The Avoidant Writer: Discussion and Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by Kim Marsh\, The Open Book Company\nWhat are you 
 avoiding when it comes to your writing? \nWriters of all genres\, 
 interests\, and experience levels are welcome to join this two-part 
 reflective workshop.\n\nWe’ve all experienced shame\, self-doubt\, and 
 fear when it comes to sharing our words with others. \n\nWhat does it feel 
 like to name those emotions and our own inner critics? What does it look 
 like to examine what we may be avoiding because of it? \n\nAre you ready to 
 explore the stories you’ve been putting off or keeping tucked away? 
 \n\nThe session will be conducted in two parts. \n\nPart 1: A Brief 
 Discussion and Q&A. Join book coach and editor Kim Marsh as she facilitates 
 a discussion about the vulnerability of sharing your stories (and what goes 
 on behind-the-scenes) with the world. \n\nPart 2: A Journaling Workshop. 
 Following the discussion and Q&A\, the time will become yours for 
 independent writing. You will be provided with a few “avoidant writer” 
 prompts and have an opportunity to reflect on something (writing-related or 
 otherwise) you have been avoiding. While an outcome might be more clarity 
 on how to move forward\, the goal is simply to reflect and explore. \n\nNo 
 preparation required. Please bring your preferred writing tools: notebook\, 
 pen\, and/or laptop etc. \n\nThis workshop is here as a reminder that none 
 of us are truly alone on this (writing) journey. \n\nKim Marsh is a writing 
 & book coach and editor. She founded The Open Book Company to help 
 individuals find\, hone and use their voice. She does this through a 
 coaching practice rooted in empathy\, authenticity\, and self-compassion. 
 The authors she works with go on to publish books with impact\, meaning\, 
 and purpose.\n\nIn addition to providing one-on-one coaching\, editing 
 services and publishing support\, Kim runs a global writing community\, 
 creating a space for grounding and accountability to anyone experiencing 
 self-doubt or a desire for more support when it comes to their writing 
 process. Kim firmly believes you don’t need a major book deal\, a spot on 
 a global stage or a PhD in English Lit to have a story worth telling. She 
 is the editor (and a contributing author) of the anthology Avoided No More: 
 On Writing Through Struggle\, Shame\, and Self-Doubt and launched her indie 
 publishing imprint\, Plymouth James Press\, in 2025. She lives in 
 Montclair\, NJ.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Writing
UID:LibCal-10306-17135631
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17135631
END:VEVENT
