SUMMARY:The Corner Book Club Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively\, librarian-led discussion of 
 award-winning author Claire Keegan's novel\, Small Things like These.  It 
 is 1985 in a small Irish town. During the weeks leading up to Christmas\, 
 Bill Furlong\, a coal merchant and family man faces into his busiest 
 season. Early one morning\, while delivering an order to the local 
 convent\, Bill makes a discovery which forces him to confront both his past 
 and the complicit silences of a town controlled by the church.  
 Registration is recommended.
LOCATION:Montclair Bellevue Avenue Branch
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Bellevue Avenue Branch":MAILTO:branch-events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Bellevue Avenue Branch, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-17701654
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17701654
END:VEVENT
