SUMMARY:November Book Club: London Falling
DESCRIPTION:A book club for adults who want to read in community. We meet 
 one Friday morning a month to chat about a title we read in 
 common.\n\n--\nNonfiction November\n\nLONDON FALLING: A MYSTERIOUS DEATH IN 
 A GILDED CITY AND A FAMILY'S SEARCH FOR TRUTH\nby Patrick Radden Keefe 
 (2026)\n\nA London family devastated by the death of their teen son 
 discovers that he had been posing as the son of a Russian oligarch\, in 
 this riveting work of narrative nonfiction by New Yorker reporter Patrick 
 Radden Keefe.\n\nCopies will be available at the Circulation Desk starting 
 October 23.
LOCATION:Literacy Room\, West Orange Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-10341-17302632
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17302632
