DTSTART:20261120T183000Z
DTEND:20261120T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261120T000000Z
SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] World of Film with Mark Phelan
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nThree Colours: Blue (1993) | 
 R\n\nJulie is haunted by her grief after living through a tragic auto wreck 
 that claimed the life of her composer husband and young daughter. Her 
 initial reaction is to withdraw from her relationships\, lock herself in 
 her apartment and suppress her pain. But avoiding human interactions on the 
 bustling streets of Paris proves impossible\, and she eventually meets up 
 with Olivier\, an old friend who harbors a secret love for her\, and who 
 could draw her back to reality.\n\nABOUT THE INSTRUCTOR\nMARK PHELAN - I am 
 a lifelong film fanatic who eats\, breathes\, sleeps and drinks movies. I 
 have studied with Donald Spoto at the New School in NYC and have a BA and 
 MA in Speech and Theatre from MSU. I have also worked as an actor and have 
 directed several plays in local regional and community theaters\, including 
 the Whole Theatre in Montclair and the Paper Mill Playhouse in Millburn\, 
 NJ. I am currently working as an adjunct professor teaching\, among other 
 courses\, Introduction to Cinema.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by 
 the MILL. Please register for classes directly through their website 
 here.\n\nFor questions about MILL classes please call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL 
 @ MPL is made possible through a partnership between the MILL\, Montclair 
 Public Library and Partners for Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater
UID:LibCal-10306-16678865
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16678865
END:VEVENT
