X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Libcal Bccls 10306": "https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15348446"}
X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10306
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10306
DTSTART:20261121T190000Z
DTEND:20261121T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261121T000000Z
SUMMARY:[Outside Org]  Aging in Montclair Saturday Social
DESCRIPTION:Program Title\n\nYankee Stadium: From the (Organ) Bench with Ed 
 Alstrom\n\nProgram Description\n\nJoin Aging in Montclair (AIM) for a 
 special behind-the-scenes look at Yankee Stadium with Ed Alstrom\, the New 
 York Yankees' longtime weekend organist.\n\nNow in his 23rd season at 
 Yankee Stadium\, Ed will share fascinating stories from the organ bench\, 
 demonstrate how he brings music to life during games\, and reveal how his 
 performances enhance the excitement and atmosphere of America's favorite 
 pastime.\n\nA graduate of Westminster Choir College\, Ed has enjoyed an 
 extraordinary musical career. He has performed with legendary artists 
 including Bette Midler\, Chuck Berry\, Leonard Bernstein\, Odetta\, and 
 Dion. He also served as associate conductor for Broadway's Hairspray\, 
 directed music Off-Broadway\, and released two acclaimed blues 
 albums.\n\nWhether you're a lifelong Yankees fan\, a baseball enthusiast\, 
 or simply curious about the music behind the game\, this engaging 
 presentation offers a unique perspective on one of baseball's most beloved 
 traditions.\n\n \n\nPresented by Aging in Montclair (AIM).
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Lectures / History & Culture, Meeting, Music, Outside Organization, Personal Growth
UID:LibCal-10306-15348446
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15348446
END:VEVENT
