SUMMARY:Spotlight on New Jersey's Black Heritage Trail Through Montclair
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a recognition of New Jersey's Black Heritage Trail 
 as we celebrate the first Montclair institutions to receive the honor in 
 2024: The James Howe House\, St. Mark's United Methodist Church\, and the 
 Montclair History Center (YWCA). \n\nWe will watch a series of short videos 
 a combination of short videos on the history of all three institutions. A 
 panel of representatives from each institution moderated by Dr. Leslie 
 Wilson of Montclair State University will follow.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
