SUMMARY:Native American Sovereignty\, Tribal Recognition and Environmental Justice in NJ NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. You can register 
 here.\n\nThis class will introduce the work of the New Jersey Center for 
 Indigenous Justice (NJCIJ) at Montclair State University. The NJCIJ walks 
 in partnership with Tribal communities to re-Indigenize New Jersey by 
 immersing students in holistic educational experiences and transforming how 
 Montclair State University lives up to its responsibility to society. We 
 will explore the meanings of tribal sovereignty and give examples of how 
 our work on environmental justice exemplifies attention to tribal 
 priorities and future-oriented work defined by a need for broader healing 
 and understanding in our state.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-17224990
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17224990
END:VEVENT
