X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10341
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10341
DTSTART:20261206T190000Z
DTEND:20261206T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20261206T000000Z
SUMMARY:Folk & Blues with Tal Naccarato
DESCRIPTION:About the program\n\nA singer-songwriter and guitarist in the 
 Americana\, folk\, and blues styles\, Tal Naccarato plays solo acoustic 
 music from his original and traditional repertoire. Mixed into the 
 performance are discussions of the various music styles and demonstrations 
 of rare vintage instruments. \n\n \n\nAbout the artist\n\nTal Naccarato is 
 a vibrant composer\, songwriter\, and teaching artist whose roots stretch 
 from the medieval mountain village of Fiumefreddo\, Bruzio\, Italy\, to the 
 vibrant community of East Flatbush\, Brooklyn. His original music is a mix 
 of folk\, Americana\, rock\, and blues\, mixed with classical guitar 
 elements and a distinct bluesy swing. Tal was the first-place winner in the 
 Long Island Blues Society Solo/Duo Competition in 2023. He performs solo 
 acoustic shows\, both with original music and traditional songs.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Performance
UID:LibCal-10341-17690175
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17690175
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Campuslabs Montclair": "https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12657859"}
X-SOURCE-ID:campuslabs_montclair
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:Arts
DESCRIPTION:Maurice Ravel’s L’enfant et les sortilèges is a wildly imagina
 tive fantasy opera where a single child’s tantrum sets an entire enchante
 d world into motion. In a flash of frustration\, the ordinary becomes ext
 raordinary—walls start to whisper\, teacups burst into song\, animals arg
 ue back\, and the child’s room transforms into a living\, breathing world
  of magic and mischief.\nAs this fantastical realm awakens\, the child is
  swept into a dazzling swirl of musical surprises and unexpected voices\,
  where every object has something to say and nothing is quite as it seems
 . With Ravel’s shimmering\, kaleidoscopic score at its heart\, this encha
 nting opera is a playful journey through wonder\, chaos\, and the power o
 f imagination to transform everything it touches.\n(Sung in French with E
 nglish Surtitles~ runtime: approx 1 hour)\nMontclair State University Stu
 dents FREE with ID at Kasser Box Office\n\nHosted by: The College of the 
 Arts\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campusl
 abs.com/engage/event/12657859
DTEND:20261206T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T061455Z
DTSTART:20261206T220000Z
LOCATION:Alexander Kasser Theater
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Chamber Opera Performance: "L'enfant et les Sortilèges"
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12657859
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12657859
X-HOSTS:The College of the Arts
END:VEVENT
