DESCRIPTION:Clear out your closets and find something new for you at the E
 nvironmental Club's Thrift & Gift event! This is your chance to swap gent
 ly used clothing\, books\, art supplies and other items with others\, all
  while supporting sustainability and reducing waste. ALL OF THESE IS FREE
 !!!\nDate: December 7thTime: 2:10 PM - 3:10 PMLocation: Center of Environ
 mental and Life Science (CELS)\, Room 110\nBring your pre-loved items to 
 trade or browse and see what catches your eye. It’s a great way to refres
 h your wardrobe\, find a new favorite book\, or stock up on art supplies 
 without spending a dime. Enjoy a fun\, friendly atmosphere\, meet new peo
 ple and give old items a new life.\nLet’s come together to create a more 
 sustainable community. We can't wait to see you there! ♻️✨\nPS: There is 
 going to be free snacks\, sodas and plushies. In addition\, you don't nee
 d to bring anything to the event to get the items. \n\nHosted by: Environ
 mental Club\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.
 campuslabs.com/engage/event/12978512
