SUMMARY:Understanding Dementia: an Overview for Caregivers w/ Alzheimer's New Jersey®
DESCRIPTION:This program is designed to provide caregivers with a 
 comprehensive overview of Alzheimer’s disease and other types of 
 dementia. Caregivers of individuals with dementia will learn about the 
 various stages of Alzheimer’s disease\, the process of getting a 
 diagnosis\, strategies for caring for someone with dementia\, and much 
 more.\n\nAdult Program | in-person | RSVP requested*\n*Open to ALL\n\nAbout 
 the presenter: For over 40 years\, Alzheimer’s New Jersey® has been here 
 for our local communities\, providing support to families impacted by 
 Alzheimer’s disease and other types of dementia. As the leading 
 Alzheimer’s organization in New Jersey\, they help local families who are 
 affected by Alzheimer’s disease and other dementias have the best days 
 possible through programs and community partnerships that increase 
 awareness and access to services.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge - Meeting Room\, Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
