DTSTART:20270115T000000Z
DTEND:20270115T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20270114T000000Z
SUMMARY:Time\, Truth\, and Yesteryear: In Conversation with Caro Claire Burke
DESCRIPTION:Join us online for a provocative and darkly humorous online 
 conversation with author Caro Claire Burke as we dive into the debut book 
 everyone’s been buzzing about–Yesteryear\, a GMA Book Club Pick and one 
 of New York Times Best Books of the Year.\n\nNatalie lives a traditional 
 lifestyle. Her charming farmhouse is rustic\, her husband a handsome 
 cowboy\, her six children each more delightful than the last. So what if 
 there are nannies and producers behind the scenes\, her kitchen hiding 
 industrial-grade fridges and ovens\, her husband the heir to a political 
 dynasty? What Natalie’s followers—all 8 million of them—don’t know 
 won’t hurt them. And The Angry Women? The privileged\, Ivy League\, 
 coastal elite haters who call her an antifeminist iconoclast? They’re 
 sick with jealousy. Because Natalie isn’t simply living the good life\, 
 she’s living the ideal—and just so happens to be building an empire 
 from it.\n\nUntil one morning she wakes up in a life that isn’t hers. Her 
 home\, her husband\, her children—they’re all familiar\, but 
 something’s off. Her kitchen is warmed by a sputtering fire rather than 
 electricity\, her children are dirty and strange\, and her soft-handed 
 husband is suddenly a competent farmer. Just yesterday Natalie was curating 
 photos of homemade jam for her Instagram\, and now she’s expected to haul 
 firewood and handwash clothes until her fingers bleed. Has she become the 
 unwitting star of a ruthless reality show? Could it really be time travel? 
 Is she being tested by God? By Satan? When Natalie suffers a brutal injury 
 in the woods\, she realizes two things: This is not her beautiful life\, 
 and she must escape by any means possible.\n\nA gripping\, electrifying 
 novel that is as funny as it is frightening\, Yesteryear is a gimlet-eyed 
 look at tradition\, fame\, faith\, and the grand performance of 
 womanhood.\n\nRegister now for the chance to participate!\n\n \n\nAbout the 
 Author:\n\nCARO CLAIRE BURKE received her Master’s in Fine Arts from the 
 Bennington Writing Seminars. She is the co-host of Diabolical Lies\, a 
 politics and culture podcast. Yesteryear is her first novel.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10286-17913700
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17913700
END:VEVENT
