DTEND:20270126T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20270125T000000Z
SUMMARY:Silent Book Club (West Essex Chapter)
DESCRIPTION:Silent Book Club is a global community of readers with nearly 
 2\,000 chapters in 55  countries. There's no assigned reading — it's 
 bring your own book.\n\nMore than a million members gather in person\, 
 online\, and in destinations around the world to read together and swap 
 stories. All readers are welcome!\n\nHOW IT WORKS: Bring your own book. 
 Grab a seat.  Enjoy a quiet reading hour. \n\nThere are no assigned 
 readings\, no pressure to socialize. All book formats are welcome 
 (headphones for audiobooks). \n\nFrom 5:30-6pm\, participants arrive\, find 
 their seats and chat with other book lovers about what you are reading. 
 \n\nFrom 6-7pm\, please enjoy the quiet reading hour and from 7-7:30pm you 
 can continue to read or socialize. \n\nMore info: 
 https://bookclubs.com/clubs/6085923/join/676f73/
LOCATION:West Caldwell - New Book Area
ORGANIZER;CN="West Caldwell Public Library":MAILTO:programs@westcaldwell.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Book Club
UID:LibCal-10340-15968879
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15968879
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Libcal Bccls 10286": "https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17980357"}
X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10286
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10286
DTSTART:20270125T230000Z
DTEND:20270126T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20270125T000000Z
SUMMARY:The "Blues" – A History of the 20th Century's Most Influential Folk Music
DESCRIPTION:The Blues was a form of regional Black Folk Music composed of 
 African rhythms\, the musical structure of the English/ Scottish song\, the 
 acoustic guitar and the Black version of the English language. It is 
 generally\, but not exclusively\, associated with the Mississippi-Yazoo 
 Delta’s cotton plantation workers\, those that built the levees along the 
 Mississippi\, the stevedores and the convicts from the 
 penitentiaries.\n\nJoin 20th century music expert\, John Groom\, as he 
 explores the early roots of the Blues and the way it has influenced music 
 and culture for generations.\n\nBio: \n\nAdult Program | in-person\nOPEN to 
 all
LOCATION:Glen Ridge - Meeting Room\, Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Music/Dance
UID:LibCal-10286-17980357
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17980357
END:VEVENT
