DESCRIPTION:**3rd Annual Mitzvah Day**  \n  \nGather as a community in ser
 vice to perform mitzvot for our local social action partners\, Israel\, an
 d Shomrei itself. All ages welcome! There is a Mitzvah for everyone\, incl
 uding kids! Babysitting available for 1st grade and under. Breakfast nosh 
 provided.  \n  \nOpen to Shomrei Community &amp\; Your Friends.  \n  \n**P
 articipate in any or all activities:**   \n  \nDONATE SUPPLIES** Donate i
 tems needed to make our Mitzvot a reality. Visit our online wish list to m
 ake a purchase. Make sure items are delivered to Shomrei **by February 3.
 ** Drop-offs at Shomrei are welcome. Or\, fund the supplies with a moneta
 ry donation. You don't have to donate items to participate (but it helps!
 )  \n**Online wish list:** (link tba)  \n**Alternative monetary donation:*
 * (link tba)  \n **VOLUNTEER YOUR TIME on February 7:**  \n\n- (Specific 
 activities tba)\n\n  \n**RSVP:** (link tba)   \n  \n**PARTICIPATE IN A DR
 IVE**  \nBring breakfast cereals and/or adult and children’s summer clo
 thing for Human Needs Food Pantry to Shomrei (Drop off at Shomrei or bring
  with you on Mitzvah Day.)  \n  \nKey fob required for building entry.  \n
    \n**Questions?**  \nContact the Office  \noffice@shomrei.org  \n(973) 
 746-5031\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260918T175100Z
LOCATION:Social Hall
TRANSP:OPAQUE
